WEBVTT

1
00:00:16.344 --> 00:00:18.765
Soon Jean Valjean was arrested in Paris.

2
00:00:19.406 --> 00:00:22.828
The newspapers were full of stories about this notorious convict.

3
00:00:23.708 --> 00:00:29.131
Here is part of a story from the Journal de Paris: This villain had succeeded in hiding from

4
00:00:29.151 --> 00:00:30.432
the police for many years.

5
00:00:31.176 --> 00:00:36.200
Changing his name to Madeleine, he had even managed to become mayor in one of our small cities

6
00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:36.820
to the north.

7
00:00:37.581 --> 00:00:43.605
He had established a very successful business, but he was finally identified and arrested, thanks to the hard

8
00:00:43.665 --> 00:00:44.525
work of the police.

9
00:00:45.486 --> 00:00:51.370
Unfortunately he escaped, but he was recaptured getting out of one of the small vehicles that travel between

10
00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:52.551
Paris and Montfermeil.

11
00:00:53.351 --> 00:00:57.875
It is said that he used his days of freedom to withdraw a large sum that he had

12
00:00:57.915 --> 00:00:59.576
deposited with one of our bankers.

13
00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:04.364
The amount is estimated at six hundred to seven hundred thousand francs.

14
00:01:05.785 --> 00:01:09.508
According to notes from his trial, he has hidden the money somewhere.

15
00:01:10.049 --> 00:01:13.452
Thus it has proven impossible for the government to seize it.

16
00:01:14.453 --> 00:01:17.235
Valjean went to trial for the robbery of the chimney sweep.

17
00:01:17.676 --> 00:01:21.499
He made no attempt to defend himself and was swiftly found guilty.

18
00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:26.624
Although he was condemned to death, Valjean refused to appeal his case.

19
00:01:27.084 --> 00:01:31.346
But the king decided to change his sentence to hard labor in prison for life.

20
00:01:32.246 --> 00:01:37.689
Valjean was sent to a prison ship in Toulon and became known as Number 9430.

21
00:01:38.549 --> 00:01:43.211
In the following months, the factory and the city where he had been mayor rapidly declined.

22
00:01:44.211 --> 00:01:49.554
Toward the end of October in that same year, the warship Orion arrived in the port of Toulon.

23
00:01:50.574 --> 00:01:54.796
The ship had long been in bad condition and had come to the city for repairs.

24
00:01:56.156 --> 00:02:01.438
Aboard the ship, along with some sailors, were some convicts who had been sentenced to hard labor.

25
00:02:02.338 --> 00:02:06.799
The arrival of the massive warship quickly attracted a large crowd of curious onlookers.

26
00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:12.101
Each day, as the repair work continued, people came to admire the vessel.

27
00:02:13.041 --> 00:02:16.682
One morning the crowd that was gazing at the ship witnessed an accident.

28
00:02:17.223 --> 00:02:21.344
The crew was taking in the sails when one of the sailors suddenly lost his balance.

29
00:02:22.252 --> 00:02:26.035
The crowd on the wharf shouted a cry of dismay as the man began to fall.

30
00:02:26.936 --> 00:02:31.960
He managed to grasp one of the ropes, but he was suspended helplessly high above the deck.

31
00:02:32.641 --> 00:02:34.382
The sea lay far below him.

32
00:02:34.863 --> 00:02:39.887
The shock of his fall had caused the rope to swing violently, and the poor man dangled at

33
00:02:39.927 --> 00:02:41.248
the end of this line.

34
00:02:42.229 --> 00:02:44.751
To go to his aid was to risk your own life.

35
00:02:46.032 --> 00:02:50.876
None of the crew, who had only recently joined the service, even dared to attempt helping him.

36
00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:54.902
In the meantime the unfortunate sailor was becoming exhausted.

37
00:02:55.903 --> 00:02:59.685
Every attempt he made to climb back up only increased the swinging of the rope.

38
00:03:00.085 --> 00:03:03.967
He did not cry out, perhaps because he did not want to waste the energy.

39
00:03:04.808 --> 00:03:08.110
It was clear to the crowd that soon he would lose his grip and fall.

40
00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:14.073
Some people on the dock had already turned away because they did not want to witness this horrible

41
00:03:14.133 --> 00:03:19.176
scene. Suddenly a man shot up the rigging with the agility of a monkey.

42
00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:24.661
The man was dressed in red, which meant he was a convict, and he wore a green cap,

43
00:03:25.121 --> 00:03:26.982
a sign that he was a prisoner for life.

44
00:03:27.982 --> 00:03:32.964
As the convict climbed, a gust of wind blew off his cap and showed that he had white

45
00:03:33.024 --> 00:03:35.424
hair. This was not a young man.

46
00:03:36.464 --> 00:03:41.806
At the first cry of alarm, the convict had run to the nearest officer and asked permission to

47
00:03:41.886 --> 00:03:43.066
save the sailor's life.

48
00:03:43.866 --> 00:03:49.368
No one else onboard dared to risk such a dangerous job, so the officer granted the convict permission.

49
00:03:50.912 --> 00:03:55.574
With one blow of a hammer, the convict broke the heavy chain that was attached to the iron

50
00:03:55.654 --> 00:03:56.654
ring around his ankle.

51
00:03:57.494 --> 00:04:03.136
Only later would the sailors remember the man's amazing strength, how easily he had broken the chain.

52
00:04:04.157 --> 00:04:09.979
Swiftly the convict climbed the mast and stood upon the yard—a wooden support for the ship's rigging.

53
00:04:10.459 --> 00:04:13.260
He paused for a few seconds to assess the situation.

54
00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:19.803
Those seconds felt like ages to the nervous onlookers below, who were watching the wind blow the sailor

55
00:04:19.843 --> 00:04:21.683
at the end of the rope back and forth.

56
00:04:22.584 --> 00:04:27.146
At last the convict took a step forward, and the crowd held its breath as one.

57
00:04:27.566 --> 00:04:30.007
He ran along the yard until he reached its tip.

58
00:04:30.427 --> 00:04:33.589
Then he fastened a rope to the yard and let it hang down.

59
00:04:34.449 --> 00:04:36.710
What happened next terrified the crowd.

60
00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:39.791
The convict began to slowly climb down the rope.

61
00:04:41.092 --> 00:04:47.217
Now, instead of seeing one man dangle at that frightening height, the crowd watched two men dangle!

62
00:04:48.158 --> 00:04:50.480
Every eye was fixed upon that pair.

63
00:04:50.961 --> 00:04:55.105
Not a word was spoken; the same emotion furrowed every brow.

64
00:04:56.026 --> 00:05:00.890
Every person held his or her breath, as if afraid to add the smallest whisper to the wind

65
00:05:00.970 --> 00:05:02.932
that was swaying the sailor and the convict.

66
00:05:03.853 --> 00:05:06.696
At last the white-haired convict reached the sailor.

67
00:05:07.384 --> 00:05:12.706
One minute more and the unfortunate sailor, exhausted and despairing, would have fallen into the sea.

68
00:05:13.666 --> 00:05:17.807
The convict secured him to the rope with one hand while clinging to it with the other.

69
00:05:18.607 --> 00:05:23.248
Finally he was seen climbing to the yard and hauling the sailor after him.

70
00:05:23.869 --> 00:05:28.370
Once there, the convict held the sailor for an instant to let him recover his strength.

71
00:05:29.290 --> 00:05:34.251
Then the older man carried the poor sailor across the yard to the mast, where he left the

72
00:05:34.311 --> 00:05:37.804
sailor in the hands of fellow seamen.

73
00:05:37.824 --> 00:05:39.826
The crowd burst into applause.

74
00:05:40.346 --> 00:05:43.548
Old officers wept, and women hugged each other on the wharf.

75
00:05:44.469 --> 00:05:48.772
On all sides voices were heard exclaiming, "That convict is a hero!

76
00:05:49.093 --> 00:05:50.634
He must be pardoned at once!"

77
00:05:51.594 --> 00:05:54.917
The convict, however, made a point of returning immediately to work.

78
00:05:55.778 --> 00:06:00.501
In order to go more quickly, he slid down the rigging and ran along the yard of a

79
00:06:00.561 --> 00:06:01.282
lower sail.

80
00:06:02.242 --> 00:06:03.924
All eyes were still following him.

81
00:06:04.520 --> 00:06:09.724
Then came the moment when all the witnesses felt alarmed because they thought they saw him hesitate and

82
00:06:09.764 --> 00:06:11.805
stagger. What was wrong?

83
00:06:12.226 --> 00:06:15.368
Did he feel tired, or was his head swimming from the heights?

84
00:06:16.109 --> 00:06:17.890
Suddenly the crowd cried out in horror.

85
00:06:18.290 --> 00:06:20.232
The convict had fallen into the sea!

86
00:06:21.172 --> 00:06:26.937
The frigate Algeciras was moored close to the Orion, and the convict plunged between the two ships.

87
00:06:28.378 --> 00:06:31.340
It was feared that he would be sucked under one or the other of the ships.

88
00:06:31.824 --> 00:06:33.626
Four men jumped into a boat at once.

89
00:06:34.126 --> 00:06:38.570
The people cheered them on, and once again anxiety took hold of everyone.

90
00:06:39.450 --> 00:06:41.492
The man did not rise to the surface.

91
00:06:42.113 --> 00:06:46.136
He simply disappeared into the sea without making even a ripple.

92
00:06:46.977 --> 00:06:51.140
The water was searched for his body until nightfall, but it was all in vain.

93
00:06:51.881 --> 00:06:53.442
His body was never recovered.

94
00:06:53.922 --> 00:07:00.468
The next morning the Toulon newspaper reported the incident and concluded: "The convict is presumed drowned.

95
00:07:01.352 --> 00:07:05.515
This man was registered under the number 9430, and his name was Jean Valjean."
